# Approval

CLI with no flags is a **dry-run**: live `awaiting_shipment` → counts + process names. It does **not** write Packing Input, catalogs, or Output.

`--run` writes one CSV per process into Packing Input **only** when the supervisor already said **run**, into the shift they named. `RESEND` / `UNMATCHED` land in that shift folder.

**Chat fast path (locked 2026-10-07, shift ask 2026-10-14):** when the supervisor says **run the group sorter** / **group my awaiting shipment** / **run the sorter** (or clear equivalent) **and names the shift**, the agent runs that shift **immediately** — no dry-run first, no long pre-amble. Report the log summary when done. If the shift was not named in that message, **ask which shift** and do not run yet. Asking for a dry-run only stays dry-run.

Catalogs are read-only on a grouping run. Step 2 fill is a different job (supervisor **fill / run**).
